    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by **Yordan Alvarez** (85.52) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), our clear top-tier options. **Yordan Alvarez** benefits from a plus matchup against a shaky arm in Young, maintaining an elite xwOBA that cements him as our primary anchor. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** becomes a priority start despite a slight wind penalty; his status as an elite speed threat against a slow-delivering pitcher offers immense stolen base upside, a critical lever given our emphasis on the scarcest category. **Junior Caminero** (70.19) and **Colt Keith** (69.64) also present strong value, both capitalizing on favorable platoon splits and high-leverage lineup slots to maintain consistent production.\n\nOur most difficult roster construction decision centered on the bench, where **Carson Benge** (51.46) narrowly missed the final utility spot. While **Carson Benge** offered a respectable platoon advantage against Rangel, the high-efficiency ceiling of **Lars Nootbaar** and **Kyle Schwarber** edged him out. We are maintaining a cautious approach with **Gary Sanchez** (42.91), who remains a fringe start due to a difficult matchup against P\u00e9rez, though he holds his spot by the slimmest of margins. Managers should monitor **Trea Turner** closely; while his 56.61 score is boosted by his leadoff position, he faces a tough assignment against a high-skill arm in McLean, which drags down his baseline efficiency. Ensure lineup stability, as any late defensive shifts against the projected pitchers could alter the dynamic platoon scores currently favoring **Christian Yelich** and **Nelson Velazquez**.",
